body.translated_text:
If these aggregates of the rebirth-phase were other than those aggregates of the death-phase, or if those aggregates of the death-phase were other than these of the rebirth-phase — then suffering would be made by another. But their otherness is not observed, since they remain in the relationship of cause and effect. For it will be said:
'Whatever arises dependent on something — it is not identical with that;
nor is it different from it; therefore it is neither annihilated nor eternal.' //
